Error: Cannot reassign variables declared outside of the component/hook

Variable `contextValue` is declared outside of the component/hook. Reassigning this value during render is a form of side effect, which can cause unpredictable behavior depending on when the component happens to re-render. If this variable is used in rendering, use useState instead. Otherwise, consider updating it in an effect. (https://react.dev/reference/rules/components-and-hooks-must-be-pure#side-effects-must-run-outside-of-render).

